To create a superclass in Java, you use the `class` keyword followed by the class name and curly braces. The superclass should contain common attributes and methods that will be shared by its subclasses.

Here's the basic syntax for creating a superclass:

```java
class SuperclassName {
    // Fields (attributes)
    // Constructor(s)
    // Methods
}
```

